{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>I saw</b> — butting. Three directions: west, north, and south; and the west is called ימה (seaward), because of the Great Sea, which is in the land of Israel to the west. For it speaks opposite the land of Israel, and this ram butts westward, also to its right and to its left, but not behind it, for it comes from the east, and it is written: קורא ממזרח עיט (calls the eagle from the east)." "<b>And all beasts</b> — these are not the beasts mentioned in the first vision, but rather all the kings it encountered on its path of advance."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The verse cited appears to be Isaiah 46:11, where עיט (bird of prey/eagle) is read literally; Ibn Ezra applies it typologically to the ram coming from the east."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:23.661370329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}